      FN
        COMMENT "/// Re-lex the [`NonLogicalNewline`] token at the given position in the context of a logical"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// line."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Returns a boolean indicating whether the lexer's position has changed. This could result"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// into the new current token being different than the previous current token but is not"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// necessarily true. If the return value is `true` then the caller is responsible for updating"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// it's state accordingly."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// This method is a no-op if the lexer isn't in a parenthesized context."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ## Explanation"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// The lexer emits two different kinds of newline token based on the context. If it's in a"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// parenthesized context, it'll emit a [`NonLogicalNewline`] token otherwise it'll emit a"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// regular [`Newline`] token. Based on the type of newline token, the lexer will consume and"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// emit the indentation tokens appropriately which affects the structure of the code."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// For example:"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```py"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// if call(foo"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///     def bar():"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///         pass"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Here, the lexer emits a [`NonLogicalNewline`] token after `foo` which means that the lexer"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// doesn't emit an `Indent` token before the `def` keyword. This leads to an AST which"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// considers the function `bar` as part of the module block and the `if` block remains empty."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// This method is to facilitate the parser if it recovers from these kind of scenarios so that"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// the lexer can then re-lex a [`NonLogicalNewline`] token to a [`Newline`] token which in"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// turn helps the parser to build the correct AST."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// In the above snippet, it would mean that this method would move the lexer back to the"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// newline character after the `foo` token and emit it as a [`Newline`] token instead of"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// [`NonLogicalNewline`]. This means that the next token emitted by the lexer would be an"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// `Indent` token."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// There are cases where the lexer's position will change but the re-lexed token will remain"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// the same. This is to help the parser to add the error message at an appropriate location."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Consider the following example:"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```py"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// if call(foo, [a, b"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///     def bar():"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///         pass"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Here, the parser recovers from two unclosed parenthesis. The inner unclosed `[` will call"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// into the re-lexing logic and reduce the nesting level from 2 to 1. And, the re-lexing logic"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// will move the lexer at the newline after `b` but still emit a [`NonLogicalNewline`] token."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Only after the parser recovers from the outer unclosed `(` does the re-lexing logic emit"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// the [`Newline`] token."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// [`Newline`]: TokenKind::Newline"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// [`NonLogicalNewline`]: TokenKind::NonLogicalNewline"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
