        COMMENT "/// Re-lex `r\"` in a format specifier position."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// `r\"` in a format specifier position is unlikely to be the start of a raw string."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// Instead, it's the format specifier `!r` followed by the closing quote of the f-string,"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// when the `}` is missing."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```py"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// f\"{test!r\""
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// ```"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "///"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// This function re-lexes the `r\"` as `r` (a name token). The next `next_token` call will"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// return a unclosed string token for `\"`, which [`Self::re_lex_string_token_in_interpolation_element`]"
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
        COMMENT "/// can then re-lex as the end of the f-string."
        WHITESPACE "\n    "
